# sweep: --bare
# Every way a game against the computer moves and ends, on a board with
# no clock, where Undo is offered.
expect Play the computer
tap-id play-computer
wait-for Start game
tap-id computer-side-white
tap-id computer-clock-none
tap-id start-computer
wait-for Kobo
expect White · Your move · Casual
expect Undo
# Nothing has been played, so there is nothing to take back.
tap-id take-back
expect Nothing to take back yet.
# An empty square and the computer's pieces are not the owner's to move.
tap-id square-e4
expect Your piece
tap-id square-e7
expect Your piece
expect-missing e7 →
# A piece is picked up, and another of the owner's pieces replaces it.
tap-id square-e2
expect e2 →
tap-id square-d2
expect d2 →
expect-missing e2 →
# Tapping the picked piece again puts it down.
tap-id square-d2
expect-missing d2 →
# A pawn cannot move three squares: the move is refused and the pawn
# stays picked up so the owner can try another square.
tap-id square-e2
tap-id square-e5
expect Illegal
expect e2 →
clean
shot computer-illegal
tap-id square-e4
wait-for White · Your move · Casual · Nf6
expect-missing Illegal
clean
shot computer-first-reply
# Undo takes back the owner's move and the computer's reply together.
tap-id take-back
expect White · Your move · Casual
expect-missing Nf6
tap-id take-back
expect Nothing to take back yet.
# Before both sides have moved, the game can be aborted instead of resigned.
tap-id game-menu
expect Offer draw
expect Resign
expect Abort
clean
shot computer-menu-opening
tap-id confirm-abort
expect Abort?
# The take-back nudge answered a board tap and does not follow into
# the confirmation.
expect-missing Nothing to take back yet.
expect Opening only
tap-id cancel-confirm
expect-missing Abort?
expect White · Your move
tap-id game-menu
tap-id confirm-abort
tap-id abort
wait-for Game aborted
expect New game
expect See the board
clean
shot computer-aborted
tap-id computer-again
wait-for Start game
tap-id start-computer
wait-for Kobo
tap-id square-d2
tap-id square-d4
wait-for White · Your move
# Once both sides have moved, abort is no longer offered.
tap-id game-menu
expect Offer draw
expect-missing Abort
# The computer accepts a draw at once.
tap-id offer-draw
wait-for Draw agreed
clean
shot computer-draw
# See the board keeps the final position, with the next game where Undo was.
tap-id dismiss-result
expect-missing Draw agreed
expect White · Finished · Casual
expect New game
expect-missing Undo
clean
shot computer-finished-board
# A finished board ignores taps on pieces.
tap-id square-e2
expect-missing e2 →
# New game in the finished game's corner goes back to the setup, and the
# next game starts with its menu closed.
tap-id computer-again
wait-for Start game
tap-id start-computer
wait-for White · Your move · Casual
expect-missing Offer draw
expect-missing Draw agreed
clean
shot computer-next-game
tap-id game-menu
tap-id offer-draw
wait-for Draw agreed
tap-id dismiss-result
# One Back leaves a finished game for the first screen, and the finished
# game is not offered for resuming.
tap Back
wait-for Play the computer
expect-missing Resume your game
